- Plx is within range of [1, 5]  
- Vmag is within range of [4, 7.5]  

---

These conditions align with the examples and astrophysical understanding: giants have spectral types with luminosity class III, lower absolute magnitudes (brighter intrinsically), redder colors (higher B-V), smaller parallaxes (farther away), and generally brighter apparent magnitudes if nearby. Non-giants (dwarfs) have luminosity class V, fainter absolute magnitudes, bluer colors, larger parallaxes, and fainter apparent magnitudes at similar distances.

